+# Feature Specification: Availability
+
+**Feature Branch**: n/a (main) | **Created**: 2026-11-11 | **Status**: Draft
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+
+### User Story 1 - See what can still be rented (P1)
+Desk staff give a period and optionally a kind (board or sail) and see which equipment is free for the whole period.
+**Acceptance**:
+1. Given a board and a sail, none booked, when asking for a period, then both ids are returned, sorted.
+2. Given a kind, then only equipment of that kind is returned; without a kind, all kinds.
+3. Given an item booked for any part of the period, then it is not returned; a booking that ends exactly at the period start, or starts exactly at its end, does not exclude it.
+4. Given nothing is free, then an empty list is returned.
+5. Asking never changes bookings or equipment.
+
+### Edge cases
+- Period not whole UTC days, unparseable, empty or reversed: refused with an error (same rules as quote/book).
+- A kind other than `board` or `sail`: refused with an error.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: `availability({start,end,kind?})` on the rental service returns an array of equipment ids.
+- **FR-002**: An id is returned only if the item matches `kind` (when given) and has no booking overlapping [start,end) (same overlap rule as `book`).
+- **FR-003**: Result is sorted ascending (plain string order).
+- **FR-004**: Period validated as in FR-005/FR-006 of the rental module; invalid `kind` throws.
+
+## Key Entities
+Equipment, Booking (existing); Availability query (start, end, kind?).
+
+## Success Criteria
+- SC-001: An id is listed by `availability` exactly when `book` of that item for the same period would succeed.
+
+## Assumptions
+- Sorting is default string order of ids; the result is a new array.
+- Constitution is an unfilled template; the five school rules govern.
